 "notes": {
  "2024_growth": "TIE 64785 says production 'rose 7%' to 'a record 2.8 million' b/d in 2024; today's series gives 8.2% and 2.868 (later revisions, not traced). The page gives today's figures and says the year was a record, which still holds for 2024 as written; it does not quote the 7%.",
  "2013_down9": "TIE 12291 says 'net ethane production was down 9% for the first four months in 2013'; field production gives -7.9% (EIA's 'net' production is a different measure). Not on the page.",
  "2022_premium": "TIE 53659's paragraph is inconsistent ('ethane prices averaged 80 cents per MMBtu' for 2021 is a premium, and '$1.36 ... 25% above the Henry Hub' is 22% on the monthly Henry Hub average of $6.07). The page quotes neither (plan review 18).",
  "prices": "No ethane price series is free to republish (D-60), and the plan review (5, 6) found that a gap computed between EIA's quoted ethane prices and a gas price depends on the heat-content convention and leaves out the costs of recovery, so the page quotes EIA's statements and computes no price gap."
 },
